e up to date, and that each cell is evaluated exactly once.\n   */\n  private recompute(seed: string): void {\n    const affected = new Set<string>([seed]);\n    const frontier = [seed];\n    while (frontier.length > 0) {\n      const key = frontier.pop()!;\n      for (const dependent of this.dependents.get(key) ?? EMPTY_SET) {\n        if (affected.has(dependent)) continue;\n        affected.add(dependent);\n        frontier.push(dependent);\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Count how many of each cell's inputs are themselves being recomputed.\n    const pending = new Map<string, number>();\n    const ready: string[] = [];\n    for (const key of affected) {\n      const cell = this.cells.get(key);\n      let count = 0;\n      if (cell) {\n        for (const precedent of cell.precedents) {\n          if (affected.has(precedent)) count++;\n        }\n      }\n      pending.set(key, count);\n      if (count === 0) ready.push(key);\n    }\n\n    while (ready.length > 0) {\n      const key = ready.pop()!;\n      this.evaluateCell(key);\n      for (const dependent of this.dependents.get(key) ?? EMPTY_SET) {\n        const remaining = pending.get(dependent);\n        if (remaining === undefined) continue;\n        pending.set(dependent, remaining - 1);\n        if (remaining - 1 === 0) ready.push(dependent);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /** Recomputes a single cell from its stored content. */\n  private evaluateCell(key: string): void {\n    const cell = this.cells.get(key);\n    if (!cell) return;\n    cell.value = cell.formula ? evaluate(cell.formula, this.resolve) : (cell.input as CellValue);\n  }\n}\n\nconst EMPTY_SET: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set<string>();\n\n/** Gathers every cell a formula reads, expanding ranges into their members. */\nfunction collectPrecedents(formula: Node): ReadonlySet<string> {\n  const precedents = new Set<string>();\n  walk(formula, (node) => {\n    if (node.type === 'reference') {\n      precedents.add(node.key);\n    } else if (node.type === 'range') {\n      for (const key of expandRange(node.range)) precedents.add(key);\n    }\n  });\n  return precedents;\n}\n\nfunction validateInput(key: string, value: CellInput): void {\n  const type = typeof value;\n  if (type !== 'string' && type !== 'number' && type !== 'boolean') {\n    throw new SpreadsheetError(\n      `Cannot store ${value === null ? 'null' : type} in ${key}; ` +\n        'expected a string, number, or boolean',\n    );\n  }\n  if (type === 'number' && !Number.isFinite(value as number)) {\n    throw new SpreadsheetError(`Cannot store ${String(value)} in ${key}; expected a finite number`);\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":187,"oldLines":48,"newStart":187,"newLines":87,"lines":["    * Decides whether giving `target` these `precedents` would close a cycle,","    * returning the offending chain or `null`.","    *","-   * The search runs *downstream*: it walks the cells that depend on `target`","-   * looking for one that `target` is about to read. That is equivalent to","-   * searching upstream from the precedents, but far cheaper in practice —","-   * a cell being written usually has few dependents while its upstream cone","-   * can span the whole sheet. It also bounds `set` by the same cone that","-   * {@link recompute} must visit anyway, so cycle checking never dominates.","+   * Writing `target` creates a cycle exactly when one of the cells it is","+   * about to read already depends on `target`. Two searches run at once over","+   * the same \"reads\" edges:","+   *","+   * - **forward** from the new precedents, following what each cell reads,","+   *   looking for `target`;","+   * - **backward** from `target`, following the cells that read it, looking","+   *   for one of the precedents.","+   *","+   * Either search alone would answer the question, but each is slow on a","+   * different shape of sheet: forward degrades when a chain is built","+   * top-down, backward when it is built bottom-up. Advancing them in","+   * lockstep a